Z||000000||johnmac||06-17-2001||07:39 AM||||Any suggestions on what I should check on my 86GT Auto transmission. Has over 120K miles.<P>What normally goes bad that I can redo without going to a transmission shop.<P><BR>Thanks,<P>John<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||06-17-2001||08:04 AM||||IMHO  Transmission rebuilds should be left to the professionals, unless you have lots of experience at rebuilding them (then I would consider you a professional).  Too many intricate things to put back together exactly right on a lot of work for nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||06-17-2001||08:51 AM||||Yea, leave it alone. Other than oil and filter changes there isn't much to do if it works. I replaced a 440t4 in a Buick recently and its cost was only $225. Considering the work involved in a rebuild, replacement is the only way to go, but only if your current transmission no longer works.<p>[This message has been edited by SteveJ (edited 06-17-2001).]||||reg||1
